From: MaiRat <enrico.bartky@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 08:59:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?Enumerate=20symbol-keyed=20own=20properties=20i?=
 =?UTF-8?q?n=20insertion=20order=20(=C2=A710.1.11.1)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

OrdinaryOwnPropertyKeys lists symbol keys last, in the order the property
was added to the object. Integer and string keys get that order from the
element array and the ownProperties sequence, but symbols lived in a bare
hash map keyed by the symbol's creation id, which records no insertion order
-- so getOwnPropertySymbols sorted by creation id, Reflect.ownKeys returned
raw hash order, and Object.assign copied in hash order. All three disagreed
with each other and with the spec.

Each object now records its symbol keys' insertion order (mirroring how
PropertySequence orders string keys): a key is appended when first added,
dropped on delete, and a deleted-then-readded key lands at the end while an
in-place update keeps its position. SymbolsInInsertionOrder reads that record
(reconciling any untracked symbol so a key is never dropped), and every
observable enumeration path -- getOwnPropertySymbols, Reflect.ownKeys,
Object.assign/CopyDataProperties -- goes through it.

Regressions in Track1LanguageTests; BuiltIns 2214 green, Integration 5030 of
5031 (pre-existing M8 only).
